Rule 1 (input tensor must have a floating-point or complex dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10
>>
Rule 2 (for real, non-empty inputs the values must lie in [-1, 1])
{v_1 : tensor} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10 ∨ ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0) then true else (min(v_1) ≥ -1 ∧ max(v_1) ≤ 1)
>>
Rule 3 (tensor rank and each dimension size must be non-negative)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
